From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:21:24 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [GDN] recover spec: commit window W > 1
 (VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE_W)

With VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE=recover, VLLM_GDN_SPEC_STATE_W=W (default 1) keeps
accepted records pending in the ring and folds them into the state only once
W tokens are pending; the verify replays the pending records in registers
(same FMA order), so outputs stay bit-identical to the per-token path.

- Ring rows R = W + num_spec + 1 (page layout from the shape calculator).
- Per-slot ring trackers (ring_start, num_pending) per cache group, bound with
  the KV cache by initialize_replayssm_ring_trackers (extended to GDN layers
  with uses_gdn_recover_trackers); verify and commit read them.
- Flush: the metadata builder (build and update_block_table) force-folds the
  pending records of every non-spec row (prefill chunks incl. resumed /
  preempted requests, non-spec decodes) before the forward and resets their
  trackers; a fresh request reusing a slot thereby drops its previous owner's
  trackers. GDNRecoverCommitGroup.flush(slots) does a forced fold.
- Tests: kernel multi-step W = 1..4, flush at finish/preemption and slot
  reuse; model path recover (W = 1, 2, 4) vs per_token, and recover W = 3 vs
  W = 1 across a prefill chunk reading a slot with pending records and a slot
  reused by a new request.

